module -- pushes the name onto the next row
    ModuleHeaderMultilineExposingComment exposing
    ( value
    {- pinned above the list's derived close -}
    )

-- The module header's `)` has no position in the AST: it is derived from the
-- items, one row below the last for a VERTICAL list and on the item's own row
-- for a flat one. A comment pinned above that `)` therefore survives a reparse
-- only while the output still reads as vertical, and for a ONE-item list the
-- only evidence of that is the item starting BELOW the header row.
--
-- A comment in the header makes the header box multi-line, and the coupled
-- layout used to refuse a multi-line header outright and fall back to the
-- generic flow -- which glues the list's first item onto the header's last row.
-- That erases the evidence, the derived `)` collapses back onto that row, and
-- the comment falls outside the list and detaches to column 1. Both the coupled
-- form and the `SortSymbols` hoist form only STACK, so neither ever needed a
-- one-line header; they had to be relaxed together, because each is reachable
-- from the other's output.


value =
    1
